Notes on third-party components:

1. The Gemma 4 E2B-it model (Google DeepMind) is the host model required to
   run any of this project's trained artefacts. Gemma 4 is governed by the
   Gemma Terms of Use (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms). Any redistribution
   or derivative use of the Gemma model weights themselves, separately from
   this code, must comply with that license. This repository does NOT
   redistribute Gemma weights; users must download Gemma 4 E2B-it directly
   from Google (HuggingFace / Kaggle) and accept the Gemma Terms.

2. The three published LoRA adapters (`weights/mode_off/`, `weights/mode_C/`,
   `weights/mode_D/`) and the three `training_grads.pt` files are small
   standalone PEFT / dict artefacts. They do NOT contain any portion of
   Gemma's pre-trained weights. To use them, you must separately load the
   corresponding host-model snapshot (verified by SHA-256 in FINGERPRINT.md).
   These trained artefacts are released under this repository's MIT license.

3. The five teacher critiques (`data/claudeopusQA0{1..5}.json`) were
   generated with Claude Opus 4.6 during the predecessor project
   (chenmoacr/amr_wtf, "GHOST"). They are kept here as educational reference
   material for the SFT experiment. The author considers their use within
   the scope of fair use under applicable law. Anthropic's Claude usage is
   governed by their own terms of service (https://www.anthropic.com/legal).
   If you intend to redistribute or commercialise these excerpts separately,
   please review those terms.

4. The Mode D inference output (`outputs/inference/mode_D_suppress_on.txt`,
   `outputs/inference/mode_D_suppress_off.txt`) is a derivative work
   produced by the trained Gemma + LoRA stack. Under Google's Gemma Output
   Terms, outputs are owned by the entity that ran the generation. This
   repository releases these output transcripts under MIT, but downstream
   users should review the Gemma Terms before commercial redistribution.
